{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-368875-r4519084","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Shikanjvi (Punjabi Spiced Lemonade)","sourcePageId":368875,"sourceRevision":"4519084","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:48:00Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Shikanjvi%20(Punjabi%20Spiced%20Lemonade)&oldid=4519084","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T14:16:00.540Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for lemonade","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"488f2772e842c472d4b298640a55ce1769c9edb8c209a2d2ffa5dc88d8243997","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Beverage recipes\n| Servings = 1\n| Difficulty = 1\n| Image = [[File:Shikanji- served with pomegranate,grated apple and mint.jpg|300px]]\n}}{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Shikanjvi''' is a type of traditional limeade or lemonade from the Punjab region of South Asia.<ref name=\"ref50fiyuq\">{{Citation | title=Classic cooking of Punjab | author=Jiggs Kalra, Pushpesh Pant | publisher=Allied Publishers, 2004 | isbn=978-81-7764-566-8 | url=https://books.google.com/books?id=HHrUDlo0DfEC}}</ref> While the base ingredients include lemon or lime juice, ginger juice, ice and water, ''shikanjvi'' often contains other ingredients such as salt, saffron, mint, rosewater, or cumin.<ref name=\"ref94dumez\">{{Citation | title=Indian regional classics: fast, fresh, and healthy home cooking | author=Julie Sahni | publisher=Ten Speed Press, 2001 | isbn=9781580083454 | url=https://books.google.com/books?id=nmYgmJGR2vUC | quote=''... Ginger Limeade (Shikanji) ...''}}</ref>\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* Cold water\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemons]], juiced\n* 1 small chunk of [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]] (raw if possible)\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Pour the water into a glass.\n# Add the lemon juice, ginger, sugar, salt and pepper, then shake it vigorously.\n# Serve cold.\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Recipes for lemonade]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Shikanjvi (Punjabi Spiced Lemonade)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"1","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Cold water","sourceText":"Cold water","amountText":"Cold water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 lemons, juiced","sourceText":"2 lemons, juiced","amountText":"2 lemons, juiced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 small chunk of ginger","sourceText":"1 small chunk of ginger","amountText":"1 small chunk of ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1–2 teaspoons sugar (raw if possible)","sourceText":"1–2 teaspoons sugar (raw if possible)","amountText":"1–2 teaspoons sugar (raw if possible)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ teaspoon salt","sourceText":"½ teaspoon salt","amountText":"½ teaspoon salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"½ teaspoon pepper","sourceText":"½ teaspoon pepper","amountText":"½ teaspoon pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Pour the water into a glass.","sourceText":"Pour the water into a glass.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Add the lemon juice, ginger, sugar, salt and pepper, then shake it vigorously.","sourceText":"Add the lemon juice, ginger, sugar, salt and pepper, then shake it vigorously.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Serve cold.","sourceText":"Serve cold.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"wikibooks:368875","recordId":"wikibooks-368875-r4519084","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceRevision":"4519084","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Shikanjvi%20(Punjabi%20Spiced%20Lemonade)&oldid=4519084","sourceSha256":"488f2772e842c472d4b298640a55ce1769c9edb8c209a2d2ffa5dc88d8243997","parserVersion":"wikibooks-sections-v3","quantityParserVersion":"source-prefix-v2","license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extract